packages/lhc/test/fixtures/openrouter-call.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/provider-double.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/pi-session-structure.provenance.md\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/read-only-delta.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/view-seam.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/drain-runner.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/pi-session-format.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/seam-conformance.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/view-thread.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/view-boundary.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/corrupt.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/work-handlers.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/receipt-schema.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/view-select-golden.test.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts\\npackages/lhc/reference/src-green-thread-events-v1/index.ts\\ndocs/key-insights/meta-thinking-and-tensions-braindump.md\\npackages/lhc/reference/src-green-thread-events-v1/token-counting/local-token-counter.ts\\npackages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\\ndocs/onboard/02-domain-design.md\\ndocs/onboard/01-core-concepts.md\\n\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:27:Verify capture by replaying recorded PI corpora through the converter and matching deterministic thread read-back and inspect surfaces.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:58:**AC-6.2:** Replay is deterministic: the same corpus replayed twice produces identical thread read-back. The deterministic-ID property holds through the converter, so a re-replay does not perturb IDs or ordering.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:80:- The implementation is narrow, but fixture fidelity and deterministic replay are easy to fake with shallow comparisons.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:81:- Red should pin exact read-back comparison and deterministic replay before Green implements the replay harness.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:113:| TC-6.2 | `test/verify/replay.test.ts` | Replaying the same corpus twice yields identical read-back, including deterministic IDs and order. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:137:- Evidence: replay tests assert read-back equality, deterministic re-replay, and inspect health/overview visibility.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:154:- Re-replay is deterministic.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:170:This plan maps every TC to one or more tests, assigns each to a chunk, and lays out the Red/Green sequence per chunk. The mock boundary is fixed by the tech design: the PI hook surface (fed by synthetic events and recorded corpora) and the `ModelCall` (a deterministic fake) are the only external edges; everything LHC runs real against a temp SQLite thread. Connector modules are exercised through their entry points, never mocked against each other.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:241:> Hard-kill (no `agent_end`) is covered as a deterministic-boundary golden in `turn-derivation.test.ts`: open turn left open, tolerated as a no-op on reattach (no duplication of the recorded prefix).\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:272:| TC-5.2 | Unreachable lane reported with kind+pair+fix; appears headless | two assignments: (a) `modelRegistry.find(provider, model)` fails; (b) model exists but `hasConfiguredAuth(model)`/`getAvailable()` says auth is absent; headless mode (`hasUI:false`) | report names kind, (provider,model), reason, and distinct fix (`fix assignment` vs `run login/configure auth`); emitted via headless channel and stored in `SessionState.health`, not only TUI |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:349:- **Green:** shape validation (LHC-enforced at construction) + reachability probe through `modelRegistry.find` plus configured-auth check + `ctx.ui`/headless reporting + override.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:364:No suite is skipped on auth availability — the closed-loop test (TC-4.5) uses a deterministic `ModelCall` fake, not a live provider, so it always runs.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:427:        id: \"SV-001\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:443:        evidence: \"AC-6.1 is scoped to replaying recorded PI corpora. The fixture loader states that, until M0 delivers recordings, it builds synthetic stand-ins (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-4`), and each named corpus source is an in-memory `AgentMessage[]` built with `makeUserMessage` / `makeAssistantMessage` (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:21-29`, `42-53`, `69-83`, `97-105`, `118-124`). The replay harness source type is also just `AgentMessage[]` (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:35-38`). During replay it synthesizes deterministic entry ids and infers `agent_end` boundaries from a new user prompt or end-of-stream (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:117-143`) instead of consuming recorded `message_end` / `agent_end` events with their original positions. That proves the converter on synthetic message shapes, but not replay fidelity for recorded PI corpora or recorded lifecycle ordering.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:455:        id: \"SV-001\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:471:        evidence: \"AC-6.1 is scoped to replaying recorded PI corpora. The fixture loader states that, until M0 delivers recordings, it builds synthetic stand-ins (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-4`), and each named corpus source is an in-memory `AgentMessage[]` built with `makeUserMessage` / `makeAssistantMessage` (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:21-29`, `42-53`, `69-83`, `97-105`, `118-124`). The replay harness source type is also just `AgentMessage[]` (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:35-38`). During replay it synthesizes deterministic entry ids and infers `agent_end` boundaries from a new user prompt or end-of-stream (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:117-143`) instead of consuming recorded `message_end` / `agent_end` events with their original positions. That proves the converter on synthetic message shapes, but not replay fidelity for recorded PI corpora or recorded lifecycle ordering.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:483:        - \"AC-6.2 / TC-6.2: deterministic replay and same-thread re-replay are covered by `test/verify/replay.test.ts`; full `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify` passed with 79 tests.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:547:    planSummary: \"Story 3 (Capture Verification) implements verify/replay.ts plus its tests; net-new code only (src/verify/replay.ts impl + test/verify/replay.test.ts new). replayCorpus(corpus, threadRef) builds a real background LhcInstance via lhc.createSdk with a local observe-only fail-closed provider (verify has no pinned boundary edge to lifecycle, so it cannot import initInstance), then drives each corpus's source AgentMessages through the REAL Story-2 converter (mapMessage -> TurnAccumulator -> capture), reconstructing the PI hook stream: each message is a message_end, and an agent_end closes the LHC turn at every agent-run boundary (before a fresh user prompt, and once at end-of-stream) so PI's 'new prompt = new run' yields exactly one turn_end per run. It drains settled, reads the durable thread back via intakeStream.listEvents + inspect.overview, and compares events (kind+payload, in source order), messages (visible + byKind), and turns (closed/open) to the fixture with a readable diff — never writing the fixture's expected events to the thread, never comparing counts alone (anti-shim). A deterministic corpus-derived piSessionId ('replay:<name>') plus a per-message entryId make the converter's idempotency keys identical across replays, so the same corpus replayed into two fresh threads is byte-identical (AC-6.2). The pinned ReplayResult {matches, diff} and the (corpus, threadRef) signature are kept exactly; Corpus is unchanged. Run story gate `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify` and epic gate `verify-all` both pass (15 test files / 79 tests). Verification serves nothing to a model.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:559:        - \"test/verify/replay.test.ts :: TC-6.2 re-replay into the same thread does not perturb read-back (deterministic keys dedup)\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:583:        - \"Determinism (AC-6.2): derive piSessionId from the corpus name (not the random temp-thread path) and stamp a deterministic per-message entryId, so the converter's Tier-1 idempotency keys are identical across replays — verified by comparing two fresh threads byte-for-byte.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/010-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"1a41acb2-b247-491e-a71a-bbd7708154bd\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec57f-ce69-7181-94a1-e5916792a981\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec57f-ce69-7181-94a1-e5916792a981\",\"storyId\":\"02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation\",\"title\":\"Story 2: Event Capture and Turn Derivation\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/validate.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/state-machine.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/007-implementor.json\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/009-verify.json\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/quick-fix/002-quick-fix.json\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Verified Story 2 AC-2.1 through AC-2.8 and TC-2.1 through TC-2.9 against the current capture implementation, capture tests, LHC intake behavior, health surfacing, and configured gates. Also audited production capture paths for fake adapters/shims/placeholders.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"No-id same-content events collide and are skipped as duplicates\",\"evidence\":\"Tech design line 329 requires fallback idempotency keys to be identical for re-delivery of the same logical event and distinct across different events, using a role/timestamp/content-hash fallback. The implemented fallback in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:37-57 omits timestamp/source order and uses only blockIndex, role, kind, and content. Production hook routing in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:348-354 calls mapMessage with only piSessionId, and local MessageEndEvent in packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:36-38 carries only message, so messages without embedded entryId use the content-only fallback. Runtime changes in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts:38-48 also use the same content-only fallback. LHC skips duplicate idempotency keys in packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216. A focused production-path node run through createConnector recorded two identical user prompts separated by agent_end as only [\\\"user_prompt\\\",\\\"turn_end\\\"] with eventCount 2, proving the second finalized message and its turn_end were skipped instead of recorded.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"AC-2.8\",\"TC-2.7\",\"TC-2.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"No-id same-content events collide and are skipped as duplicates\",\"evidence\":\"Tech design line 329 requires fallback idempotency keys to be identical for re-delivery of the same logical event and distinct across different events, using a role/timestamp/content-hash fallback. The implemented fallback in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:37-57 omits timestamp/source order and uses only blockIndex, role, kind, and content. Production hook routing in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:348-354 calls mapMessage with only piSessionId, and local MessageEndEvent in packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:36-38 carries only message, so messages without embedded entryId use the content-only fallback. Runtime changes in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts:38-48 also use the same content-only fallback. LHC skips duplicate idempotency keys in packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216. A focused production-path node run through createConnector recorded two identical user prompts separated by agent_end as only [\\\"user_prompt\\\",\\\"turn_end\\\"] with eventCount 2, proving the second finalized message and its turn_end were skipped instead of recorded.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"AC-2.8\",\"TC-2.7\",\"TC-2.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-2.1 / TC-2.1: user, assistant, and toolResult sequence records in source order; assistant fan-out thinking -> text -> tool_call is covered by packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts.\",\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2 / TC-2.3: PI per-step turn_end is ignored, one LHC turn_end is emitted at agent_end, and repeated turnIndex 0 runs order by source order in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts.\",\"AC-2.3 / TC-2.4: parallel tool results arriving b then a retain toolCallId correlation in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts.\",\"AC-2.4 / TC-2.5: isError tool result records tool_result with error flag and content in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts.\",\"AC-2.5 / TC-2.6: graceful interrupt records partial assistant content, carries aborted disposition via runtime_note, and closes at agent_end in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts.\",\"AC-2.7 / TC-2.8: writable malformed input records a durable capture gap surfaced by inspect.health; unavailable store records extension health without throwing in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts.\",\"AC-2.8 / TC-2.9 partial: model_select and thinking_level_select each produce ordered runtime_note events with new and previous values for the covered single-change scenario in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-2.1 / AC-2.6: every finalized no-id PI message is not proven because repeated same-content messages collide on the content-only fallback and the later event is skipped.\",\"AC-2.6 / TC-2.7: idempotency distinctness for different no-id events is unmet; current tests prove same-key replay skips, but not that distinct same-content events get distinct keys.\",\"AC-2.8 / TC-2.9: repeated identical runtime changes are not proven because runtime_note keys are content-only and will collide.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"focused node production-path proof: createConnector records two identical user prompts separated by agent_end\",\"result\":\"fail\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Production capture path still uses content-only fallback idempotency keys for no-id messages and runtime changes, so distinct same-content events can be skipped by LHC duplicate-key handling.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"No material fake adapter, mock path, shim, or placeholder was found in the Story 2 capture production path. Out-of-scope NotImplemented stubs remain in later-story modules, and the default observe-only provider fails closed rather than fabricating derived content.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/010-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T09:39:07.400Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T09:44:25.670Z\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/06-startup-validation-and-assignment-config/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:39:- Shipped default assignments.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/06-startup-validation-and-assignment-config/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:68:**AC-5.4:** Model assignments load from the extension's config. Each of the seven derivation kinds resolves to 