startup-validation-and-assignment-config is ready to start a composed run.\",\"evidence\":[]},{\"name\":\"baseline-seed\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"Captured deterministic pre-story baseline seed (394 matching test file(s)).\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context\"]}],\"blockers\":[],\"notes\":[\"Ignored non-story markdown files in stories/: coverage.md\",\"codex auth status unknown — proceed if CLI works in your environment.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/06-startup-validation-and-assignment-config/001-story-validate.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T13:05:35.906Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T13:05:36.417Z\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/06-startup-validation-and-assignment-config/006-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"9e175873-c96c-466a-9c07-f739be95e8fe\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec645-93ad-7391-a7e4-a6549c4e972d\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec645-93ad-7391-a7e4-a6549c4e972d\",\"storyId\":\"06-startup-validation-and-assignment-config\"},\"mode\":\"followup\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"06-startup-validation-and-assignment-config\",\"title\":\"Story 6: Startup Validation and Assignment Config\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/06-startup-validation-and-assignment-config.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/quick-fix/011-quick-fix.json\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/assignments.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/startup-validation.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/inference/assignments.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/inference/startup-validation.test.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Follow-up verification focused on SV-001 through SV-005 after quick-fix/011, directly touched Story 6 code/tests, focused Story 6 tests, and configured story/epic gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"status\":\"still-open\",\"rationale\":\"The literal `unconfigured` placeholder is gone and defaults are now validated, but the shipped default is now `deterministic/default` in `defaultAssignments`. The production SDK path still uses `createModelCall(ctx)`, which resolves assignments through PI `ctx.modelRegistry.find(provider, model)`, not LHC's deterministic provider. No evidence shows `deterministic/default` is a real PI registry lane for the extension user, so AC-5.4's shipped defaults-function requirement remains unproven and appears to rely on a local verification lane.\"},{\"id\":\"SV-002\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"rationale\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/assignments.ts now rejects unknown keys before merging, and direct proof showed `loadAssignments({made_up_kind:{...}})` throws `Unknown assignment key 'made_up_kind'`. The assignments test also covers this path.\"},{\"id\":\"SV-003\",\"status\":\"still-open\",\"rationale\":\"The report now stores a formatted `message` in `SessionState.health`, but `report()` still only calls `ctx.ui.notify` when `ctx.hasUI` is true and has no headless log/output branch. The headless test asserts state text and no UI notify, not an emitted headless channel.\"},{\"id\":\"SV-004\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"rationale\":\"packages/pi-lhc/test/inference/startup-validation.test.ts now captures messages, drains the scheduler, and asserts failed `smoothed_prompt` plus queryable `inspect.health` failure details for the affected lane. Focused tests passed.\"},{\"id\":\"SV-005\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"rationale\":\"`pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify` and `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all` both passed with 20 test files and 140 tests.\"}],\"newFindings\":[],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Shipped defaults still are not proven production-reachable PI lanes\",\"evidence\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts:152-154 now defaults all assignments to `{ provider: \\\"deterministic\\\", id: \\\"default\\\" }`; direct proof returned `{provider:\\\"deterministic\\\",model:\\\"default\\\",prompt:\\\"smoothing-v1\\\"}` for `loadAssignments(undefined).smoothed_prompt`. But packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts still builds production inference with `call: createModelCall(ctx)` and those assignments, and packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts:99-109 resolves every assignment through `ctx.modelRegistry.find(provider, model)`. No code path activates LHC's deterministic provider for these defaults, and no artifact proves PI's production registry contains `deterministic/default`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/assignments.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/inference/assignments.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.4\",\"TC-5.4\",\"Real-Code Workaround Standard\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Headless unreachable-lane reporting still has no emitted headless channel\",\"evidence\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/startup-validation.ts:91-118 marks the flag and stores the formatted message in `state.health.startupValidation`, but only emits via `ctx.ui.notify` under `if (ctx.hasUI)`. There is no `else` branch or injected output/log channel for headless mode. packages/pi-lhc/test/inference/startup-validation.test.ts:161-190 verifies stored text and explicitly expects `notify` not to be called; it does not prove a headless-mode report reaches an output channel.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/startup-validation.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/inference/startup-validation.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.2\",\"TC-5.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-5.1 / TC-5.1: validation iterates all `FORM_KINDS` and runs from `session_start` before capture hooks are used.\",\"AC-5.2 partial: unreachable reports include kind, provider/model, reason, and fix; interactive `ctx.ui.notify` path exists.\",\"AC-5.3 / TC-5.3: focused test now captures, drains derivations, and verifies affected-lane failed forms through `inspect.health`.\",\"AC-5.5 / TC-5.5: complete known-kind overrides take effect on next load.\",\"TC-5.6 partial: incomplete known-kind assignments, unknown prompt names, explicit placeholders, and unknown config keys fail loudly.\",\"Story gate passed: `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify`.\",\"Epic gate passed: `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all`.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-5.4 / TC-5.4: shipped defaults are real production PI registry lanes that let derivations function without operator config.\",\"AC-5.2 / TC-5.2: unreachable-lane report is emitted through a headless output/log channel, not only stored in health.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec vitest run test/inference/startup-validation.test.ts test/inference/assignments.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Production default assignments now use `deterministic/default`, but the production call path still routes through PI `modelRegistry.find`; no real deterministic provider is wired for the extension runtime.\",\"Headless startup-validation reporting still mutates health only; no emitted headless output/log channel is present.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"The previous gate blocker is closed; both configured gates passed.\",\"The prior TC-5.3 coverage gap is closed by the new capture/drain/inspect health test.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/06-startup-validation-and-assignment-config/006-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T13:26:21.842Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T13:28:38.094Z\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/004-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"5b238ac4-14c1-41f5-9fbe-4d6a8af4fdaf\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec5f5-8cee-73a3-a1df-64da125e5d08\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec5f5-8cee-73a3-a1df-64da125e5d08\",\"storyId\":\"04-fork-as-new-thread\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"04-fork-as-new-thread\",\"title\":\"Story 4: Fork as New Thread\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/04-fork-as-new-thread.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/001-story-validate.json\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/003-implementor.json\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/story-lead/001-current.json\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/thread.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/package.json\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Verified Story 4 against AC-3.1..AC-3.3 / TC-3.1..TC-3.3, the configured story and epic gates, fork production code, connector routing, and fork tests.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-04-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Fork routing still depends on session_start.reason === \\\"fork\\\"\",\"evidence\":\"Story TC-3.1 says fork detection must resolve from session_before_fork hook data and not from a fork reason code; tech design Flow 3 records that print-mode --fork can report reason=startup. In packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:306-350, the fork path executes only when `event.reason === \\\"fork\\\" && pendingFork !== null`; otherwise packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:350-356 runs normal launch resolution. A real fork reported as startup will not seed from the pending fork point.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.1\",\"TC-3.1\",\"AC-3.2\",\"TC-3.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-04-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"PI session-tree fallback is explicitly absent\",\"evidence\":\"Story Scope In and TC-3.1 require PI's session tree as Epic 1 fallback evidence when session_before_fork is absent. packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts:13-21 says the fallback is not implemented and returns null. packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:549-555 only records fork state from the hook, so hook-absent fallback evidence has no production path.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.1\",\"TC-3.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-04-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Seed failure continues with an empty fork thread\",\"evidence\":\"AC-3.2 / TC-3.2 require the forked thread's read-back to match the source through the fork point. packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:338-343 calls seedFork, but on failure records only `fork_seed_failed` and explicitly continues with an empty fork; packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:347-349 then resolves the target thread as the active thread. This is a real runtime fallback that can produce an unseeded fork.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"TC-3.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-04-004\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"TC-3.3 lacks proof that target forms requeue\",\"evidence\":\"TC-3.3 requires forms to requeue on the fork target and not be copied. In packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts:157-159 the source prompt is captured without the `entry-fork` entryId, then packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts:177 forks with `entryId: \\\"entry-fork\\\"`, so seeding can fail with no matching source event. packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts:184-192 contains comments but no inspect.health or target-form assertions, so the test passes without proving requeue/drain or no-copy behavior.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-04-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Fork routing still depends on session_start.reason === \\\"fork\\\"\",\"evidence\":\"Story TC-3.1 says fork detection must resolve from session_before_fork hook data and not from a fork reason code; tech design Flow 3 records that print-mode --fork can report reason=startup. In packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:306-350, the fork path executes only when `event.reason === \\\"fork\\\" && pendingFork !== null`; otherwise packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:350-356 runs normal launch resolution. A real fork reported as startup will not seed from the pending fork point.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.1\",\"TC-3.1\",\"AC-3.2\",\"TC-3.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-04-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"PI session-tree fallback is explicitly absent\",\"evidence\":\"Story Scope In and TC-3.1 require PI's session tree as Epic 1 fallback evidence when session_before_fork is absent. packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts:13-21 says the fallback is not implemented and returns null. packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:549-555 only records fork state from the hook, so hook-absent fallback evidence has no production path.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.1\",\"TC-3.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-04-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Seed failure continues with an empty fork thread\",\"evidence\":\"AC-3.2 / TC-3.2 require the forked thread's read-back to match the source through the fork point. packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:338-343 calls seedFork, but on failure records only `fork_seed_failed` and explicitly continues with an empty fork; packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:347-349 then resolves the target thread as the active thread. This is a real runtime fallback that can produce an unseeded fork.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.2\",\"TC-3.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-04-004\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"TC-3.3 lacks proof that target forms requeue\",\"evidence\":\"TC-3.3 requires forms to requeue on the fork target and not be copied. In packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts:157-159 the source prompt is captured without the `entry-fork` entryId, then packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts:177 forks with `entryId: \\\"entry-fork\\\"`, so seeding can fail with no matching source event. packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts:184-192 contains comments but no inspect.health or target-form assertions, so the 