code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial verification of Story 2 against AC-2.1 through AC-2.8, TC-2.1 through TC-2.9, current capture source/tests, production capture paths, LHC duplicate-key behavior, and configured gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"No-id, no-position capture events still collide on fallback idempotency keys\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.1 requires every finalized PI message to be recorded and AC-2.6 requires duplicate safety without dropping distinct events. The local production hook type keeps both MessageEndEvent.entryId and MessageEndEvent.position optional in packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:36-39. The hook path only supplies fallbackId from event.position when entryId is absent in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:379-385, and runtime-change hooks do the same for optional position in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:402-415. If position is absent, eventKey falls to fallbackId \\\"no-stable-id\\\" in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:54-60. Focused checks failed: two no-entryId/no-position same-text user prompts produced the identical key `pi:s:fp:no-stable-id:0:user:user_prompt:2cda7449dd14dbba9a0c9de9`, and two identical model_select events without position produced the identical key `pi:s:fp:no-stable-id:0:system:runtime_note:fad453e343e63228f9ea2f15`. LHC skips duplicate idempotency keys in packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216, so later distinct events on this production path can be skipped.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"AC-2.8\",\"TC-2.7\",\"TC-2.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"No-id, no-position capture events still collide on fallback idempotency keys\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.1 requires every finalized PI message to be recorded and AC-2.6 requires duplicate safety without dropping distinct events. The local production hook type keeps both MessageEndEvent.entryId and MessageEndEvent.position optional in packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:36-39. The hook path only supplies fallbackId from event.position when entryId is absent in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:379-385, and runtime-change hooks do the same for optional position in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:402-415. If position is absent, eventKey falls to fallbackId \\\"no-stable-id\\\" in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:54-60. Focused checks failed: two no-entryId/no-position same-text user prompts produced the identical key `pi:s:fp:no-stable-id:0:user:user_prompt:2cda7449dd14dbba9a0c9de9`, and two identical model_select events without position produced the identical key `pi:s:fp:no-stable-id:0:system:runtime_note:fad453e343e63228f9ea2f15`. LHC skips duplicate idempotency keys in packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216, so later distinct events on this production path can be skipped.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"AC-2.8\",\"TC-2.7\",\"TC-2.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-2.1 / TC-2.1: user/assistant/toolResult source-order capture and assistant thinking -> text -> tool_call fan-out are covered through the real hook -> converter -> LHC intake path in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:43-87.\",\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2: the worked example records exactly one LHC turn_end at agent_end and PI per-step turn_end hooks produce none in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:39-83.\",\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.3: two runs with repeated turnIndex 0 order by converter source-event order in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:86-118.\",\"AC-2.3 / TC-2.4: parallel out-of-order tool results correlate by toolCallId in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:39-77.\",\"AC-2.4 / TC-2.5: tool result isError and error content are captured without drop in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:80-105.\",\"AC-2.5 / TC-2.6: graceful interrupt partial content, aborted disposition runtime_note, and complete-but-aborted turn close are covered in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts:29-65.\",\"AC-2.6 / TC-2.7: stable-key re-delivery skips and normal resume without historical re-fire are covered for entryId/source-position-backed cases in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:145-191 and packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts:138-168.\",\"AC-2.7 / TC-2.8: malformed writable-thread input records a durable capture gap surfaced in